            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Gumnut&quot; device for off-pump proximal aortocoronary anastomosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>511-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8191.2007.00549.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Use of side-biting clamps in patients with coronary artery disease and atheromatous disease of ascending aorta, undergoing coronary artery surgery can lead to major postoperative neurological events. We describe the use of a simple device to avoid use of side-biting clamp on aorta for proximal aortocoronary anastomosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
